 "notes": "Single OCR'd map sheet; map face and legend read on page images. Symbols me, agn, gb, gbd, qtz, ? and my read from legend boxes. OCR '4 millimeters to | meter' read as 1 (inferred, unclear in OCR); 'gavels' read as gravels. The 'Unknown material' units are drawn on the map face in the east-central area. Folds and thrust planes are recorded from the drawn symbols near the Pacolet River (names from the legend); the many strike/dip and plunge numbers have no printed strikes or locations and were not recorded. A red 'dike of massive vein' line is drawn in the southwest but unlabelled. No ages printed except Quaternary alluvium. No drill holes, cross section or references. SUBSURFACE: none.",
